# Cache policy for the Cloudflare Workers deployment.
#
# Cloudflare Workers static assets reads this file from the assets directory;
# Vite copies everything in web/public/ into web/dist/, so it ships with the
# build. GitHub Pages ignores the file, which is harmless — it serves the same
# bundle under its own (unconfigurable) cache policy.
#
# Measured before this file existed: every response, including content-hashed
# assets, came back `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`. So each page load
# re-validated every JS and CSS chunk over the network to be told "not
# modified". Vite fingerprints those filenames by content, which is exactly the
# condition `immutable` is for — a changed file gets a changed name, so the
# cached copy can never be wrong.
#
# index.html is deliberately NOT cached: it is the one file that must be
# re-fetched to learn the current asset hashes after a deploy. Leaving it on
# `max-age=0, must-revalidate` is correct and stays the default.

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
